---
export const title = 'Grouping';
export const order = 550;
import DemoComponentCard from '../../../../components/DemoComponentCard.astro';

import dataSource from '../_data-source.json';
---

<p>
  Set <code>group-by</code> to a field name to group the rows under header rows. A group header is
  one cell across every column with a toggle button (<code>aria-expanded</code>), the group's value
  (or <code>groupTemplate(group, rows)</code>) and its row count. Rows with an empty value share the
  <em>(Empty)</em> group, which comes last.
</p>
<p>
  Groups are ordered by value; sorting applies within each group, and a sort on the grouped field
  orders the groups (descending sorts reverse them). In managed mode, groups keep the order the rows
  arrive in. <code>collapsed-groups</code> holds the collapsed groups' values as strings; the table
  updates it and fires <code>group-toggle</code> with <code>{'{ group, expanded }'}</code>.
</p>
<p>
  Group headers are rows of the arrow-key grid: <kbd>Up</kbd> and <kbd>Down</kbd> reach them, and
  <kbd>Enter</kbd> or <kbd>Space</kbd> collapses or expands the group. <kbd>Left</kbd> and
  <kbd>Right</kbd> stay on the header, and moving on keeps the column you came from. Headers count
  in <code>aria-rowcount</code> and <code>aria-rowindex</code>, which number every header and row
  across pages.
</p>
<p>
  With pagination, pages hold data rows; a group that continues on the next page repeats its header
  there. Rows of a collapsed group still count towards their page, so prefer grouping without
  pagination, or with <code>virtual</code>.
</p>

<DemoComponentCard lang='html'>
  <div style='width: 100%; height: 28rem;'>
    <wc-table id='table-grouping' key-field='_id' group-by='eyeColor' sort-by='name' label='People'></wc-table>
  </div>

  <script is:inline define:vars={{ dataSource }}>
    const $table = document.getElementById('table-grouping');
    $table.columns = [
      { name: 'name', label: 'Name', width: 14 },
      { name: 'eyeColor', label: 'Eye color', width: 10 },
      { name: 'age', label: 'Age', width: 7, type: 'number', aggregate: 'avg' },
    ];
    $table.data = dataSource;
  </script>
</DemoComponentCard>
